Internet Services

A Plug-In for Mill with four protocols. Put "Internet Services" in the
"Mill Plug-Ins" folder. If you also have the Finger example there, take it out:
both give finger:.

  finger://host/user         Finger (RFC 1288). finger://host/ asks about everyone.
  whois://host/query         Whois (RFC 3912). whois://host/ asks for a query.
  dict://host/d:word[:db]    Dictionary Server Protocol (RFC 2229): a definition.
  dict://host/m:word[:db[:strategy]]   the words that match; each links to its definition.
  time://host/               Time Protocol (RFC 868): the server's time and this Mac's.

Mill's addresses need a host, so "default" stands for a protocol's Default
server setting (Settings, Protocols): whois://default/example.com,
dict://default/d:windmill, time://default/. The defaults are whois.iana.org,
dict.org, and time.nist.gov.

time: shows the difference between the server's clock and this Mac's. "Set this
Mac's clock" adds that difference to the Mac's time when it is clicked, so it is
right however long the page has been open. Only the button on the Plug-In's own
page works. System 6 has no time zone: the Time zone setting says how many hours
the Mac's clock is from UTC (UTC-8, UTC+1), and is 0 (UTC) at first.

Build: ./build.sh (Retro68 in Docker) writes build/Internet Services.bin, a
MacBinary file. The code is one 'MPlg' 128 resource; the licence is 'TEXT' 129.
